{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To find the foot of the perpendicular from point \\(A = (1,8,4)\\) to the line passing through points \\(B = (0,-1,3)\\) and \\(C = (2,-3,-1)\\), we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Find the direction vector of the line passing through \\(B\\) and \\(C\\):**\n\n   The direction vector \\(\\vec{d}\\) can be found by subtracting the coordinates of \\(B\\) from the coordinates of \\(C\\):\n   \\[\n   \\vec{d} = C - B = (2 - 0, -3 - (-1), -1 - 3) = (2, -2, -4)\n   \\]\n\n2. **Find a parametric equation for the line:**\n\n   Using point \\(B\\) and the direction vector \\(\\vec{d}\\), the parametric equation of the line can be written as:\n   \\[\n   \\vec{r}(t) = B + t\\vec{d} = (0, -1, 3) + t(2, -2, -4) = (2t, -1 - 2t, 3 - 4t)\n   \\]\n\n3. **Find the vector from point \\(A\\) to a general point on the line:**\n\n   Let the foot of the perpendicular be \\(P = (2t, -1 - 2t, 3 - 4t)\\). The vector \\(\\vec{AP}\\) from \\(A\\) to \\(P\\) is:\n   \\[\n   \\vec{AP} = P - A = (2t - 1, -1 - 2t - 8, 3 - 4t - 4) = (2t - 1, -9 - 2t, -1 - 4t)\n   \\]\n\n4. **Set up the condition for perpendicularity:**\n\n","prefix_end":1044,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,1477,279,4478,315,279,76833,504,1459,17767,32,284,320,16,11,23,11,19,10699,8,311,279,1555,12299,1526,3501,17767,33,284,320,15,4999,16,11,18,10699,8,323,17767,34,284,320,17,4999,18,4999,16,10699,701,582,1184,311,1795,1493,7354,1447,16,13,3070,9885,279,5106,4621,315,279,1555,12299,1526,17767,33,57758,323,17767,34,59,1648,56177,256,576,5106,4621,1124,11520,4083,90,67,11035,8,646,387,1730,553,32256,287,279,13934,315,17767,33,57758,504,279,13934,315,17767,34,59,982,256,1124,9640,256,1124,4083,90,67,92,284,356,481,425,284,320,17,481,220,15,11,481,18,481,10293,16,701,481,16,481,220,18,8,284,320,17,11,481,17,11,481,19,340,256,1124,2533,17,13,3070,9885,264,1685,16340,2360