2102508545,"seed":365460205794032462,"stop":"eos","text":"To find the foot of the perpendicular from point \\(A = (1,8,4)\\) to the line passing through points \\(B = (0,-1,3)\\) and \\(C = (2,-3,-1)\\), we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Find the direction vector of the line passing through \\(B\\) and \\(C\\):**\n\n   The direction vector \\(\\vec{d}\\) can be found by subtracting the coordinates of \\(B\\) from the coordinates of \\(C\\):\n   \\[\n   \\vec{d} = C - B = (2 - 0, -3 - (-1), -1 - 3) = (2, -2, -4)\n   \\]\n\n2. **Find a parametric equation for the line:**\n\n   Using point \\(B\\) and the direction vector \\(\\vec{d}\\), the parametric equation of the line can be written as:\n   \\[\n   \\vec{r}(t) = B + t\\vec{d} = (0, -1, 3) + t(2, -2, -4) = (2t, -1 - 2t, 3 - 4t)\n   \\]\n\n3. **Find the vector from point \\(A\\) to a general point on the line:**\n\n   Let the foot of the perpendicular be \\(P = (2t, -1 - 2t, 3 - 4t)\\). The vector \\(\\vec{AP}\\) from \\(A\\) to \\(P\\) is:\n   \\[\n   \\vec{AP} = P - A = (2t - 1, -1 - 2t - 8, 3 - 4t - 4) = (2t - 1, -9 - 2t, -1 - 4t)\n   \\]\n\n4. **Set up the condition for perpendicularity:**\n\n   The vectors \\(\\vec{AP}\\) and \\(\\vec{d}\\) are perpendicular if their dot product is zero:\n   \\[\n   \\vec{AP} \\cdot \\vec{d} = 0\n   \\]\n   Substituting the vectors, we get:\n   \\[\n   (2t - 1, -9 - 2t, -1 - 4t) \\cdot (2, -2, -4) = 0\n   \\]\n   Calculate the dot product:\n   \\[\n   2(2t - 1) + (-2)(-9 - 2t) + (-4)(-1 - 4t) = 0\n   \\]\n   Simplify each term:\n   \\[\n   4t - 2 + 18 + 4t + 4 + 16t = 0\n   \\]\n   Combine like terms:\n   \\[\n   24t + 20 = 0\n   \\]\n   Solve for \\(t\\):\n   \\[\n   24t = -20 \\implies t = -\\frac{20}{24} = -\\frac{5}{6}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Find the coordinates of the foot of the perpendicular:**\n\n   Substitute \\(t = -\\frac{5}{6}\\) back into the parametric equation of the line:\n   \\[\n   P = (2t, -1 - 2t, 3 - 4t) = \\left(2\\left(-\\frac{5}{6}\\right), -1 - 2\\left(-\\frac{5}{6}\\right), 3 - 4\\left(-\\frac{5}{6}\\right)\\right)\n   \\]\n   Simplify each coordinate:\n   \\[\n   P = \\left(-\\frac{10}{6}, -1 + \\frac{10}{6}, 3 + \\frac{20}{6}\\right) = \\left(-\\frac{5}{3}, -\\frac{6}{6} + \\frac{10}{6}, \\frac{18}{6} + \\frac{20}{6}\\right) = \\left(-\\frac{5}{3}, \\frac{4}{6}, \\frac{38}{6}\\right) = \\left(-\\frac{5}{3}, \\frac{2}{3}, \\frac{19}{3}\\right)\n   \\]\n\nThus, the foot of the perpendicular is \\(\\boxed{\\left(-\\frac{5}{3}, \\frac{2}{3}, \\frac{19}{3}\\right)}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\left(-\\frac{5}{3}, \\frac{2}{3}, \\frac{19}{3}\\right)}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"precalculus:258"}
